## Level 1: future-tube theorem

Reader 2 / refuter 2: confirmed_nonfatal, completed repair confidence 1. Proof 1.2 now requires K nonempty and compact. Continuity of b0-|b spatial| on K gives a positive attained minimum; its only subsequent use takes K={b}. No theorem hypothesis or conclusion changes.

Independently checked all six steps: the Minkowski Cauchy-Schwarz estimate gives nonnegative damping in the closed cone; q0>=1/sqrt(2) on unit future vectors gives uniform exponential damping on nonempty compact subsets of the open cone. Cone restriction makes every multiplier globally bounded Borel. Exact thm-bounded-borel-pvm-integral Statement clauses 1-2 supply pairing uniqueness, norm bound and quadratic identity under AC_omega, and hence linearity. For |h|<c/2, r^2 exp(-(c-|h|)r) has a uniform finite supremum, so step 2.2 has an O(|h|^2) operator-norm remainder. The first-linear pairing preserves complex linearity. Step 3.1 uses countable annular spectral truncations and a contraction tail; it proves strong continuity also at null imaginary displacements, without a boundary operator-norm assertion. The finite product expansion in 4.1 has an O(||h||^2) remainder; n=1, zero vectors and zero insertions are covered. Exact holomorphy definition is def-cm-complex-phase-domains-and-holomorphic-maps, Definition first paragraph.

The contract derivation and empty-case worksheet were synchronized. Corrected an audit-only finite-check locator (product derivative is 4.1, n=2 has one insertion). CRITICAL risk review complete before level 2; no CPT, unbounded field or distributional continuation is inferred.

## Level 2: discrete-symmetry interface

Reader/refuter 3: confirmed_fatal. Required the same H and Omega for the joint spectral data and the full-group representation and the identity U((I,a))=U_spec(a)=Phi_E(exp(ip.a)) for every real a. Two independently supplied representations otherwise need not share their spectra. Reader/refuter 4: confirmed_fatal. Added lem-qft-poincare-pullback-continuity-on-schwartz as a mathematical dependency and stated the exact pullback through Lambda(A). Its published proof 1.1 expands the affine chain rule and monomial weights into finitely many Schwartz seminorms; 2.1-3.1 prove parameter continuity. Applied to (Lambda(A),a), its forward and inverse maps preserve Schwartz space. Reader/refuter 5: confirmed_nonfatal. Replaced the undefined exchange domain D by D_field. All three repairs complete, confidence 1.

The same-domain linear maps already type all finite products, while n-point tempered extension remains a separate requirement. The semidirect product agrees with the pullback homomorphism. Single/mixed spin parity, locality sign and component/adjoint conventions remain explicit theorem-specific obligations. This definition asserts no sufficiency theorem. Definition supplier links were preserved in the immediately following reference section; manifest and risk review synchronized. Direct item/reference search found no consumer of this interface beyond its own A-page placement. No further interface hop or outside repair arises. HIGH risk review complete.

## Level 2: finite-spectrum example

All three Verification steps independently checked; no owed decision or mathematical repair. The two atoms 0,p are distinct by p!=0. Coordinate PVM additivity is finite at each atom, U_p is strongly continuous unitary, and arbitrary first-column matrices prove cyclicity for the full matrix star-algebra. Nonzero future null momenta still have p0>0 and strictly positive pairing with open-future b. The nonzero mode damps, the vacuum remains 1 and the full operator norm is 1. Fourier sign reversal exchanges damping directions; b=0 gives modulus 1. HIGH risk review complete after the interface review.

